# Generated media. All of it is regenerable:
#   docs/iters/*.html   scripts/iter_report.py   (6-7 MB each: GIFs embedded as base64)
#   docs/videos/*       blender_render_scene.py + ffmpeg
# Committing them grows the history on every re-render for no gain over rerunning the script.
# Every docs/*.html is a generated report page with media embedded as base64 -- they run
# 0.4-7 MB each and are rewritten wholesale on each regeneration, so they bloat history
# without ever diffing usefully. The WRITTEN record lives in docs/*.md, which is what
# CLAUDE.md points at; the pages are republished as artifacts anyway.
docs/*.html
docs/iters/
docs/videos/
